  "title": "People, pronouns and \"to be\"",
  "note": "być (to be) is irregular: jestem, jesteś, jest, jesteśmy, jesteście, są. Subject pronouns are usually dropped because the verb ending shows the person. Nouns have three genders, usually visible from the ending: consonant = masculine (m), -a = feminine (f), -o/-e/-ę = neuter (n). The dictionary form is the nominative case.",
